1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,488
When a payment is slow or stuck, how would you even know?

2
00:00:03,488 --> 00:00:09,202
One payment crosses five modules and a processing center, and plain logs cannot follow it.

3
00:00:09,202 --> 00:00:16,297
Micrometer counts payments by status and times every processing call, and Prometheus collects those numbers.

4
00:00:16,297 --> 00:00:20,559
Grafana turns them into a dashboard, with alerts on timeouts.

5
00:00:20,559 --> 00:00:25,571
OpenTelemetry gives every payment a trace that follows it from module to module.

6
00:00:25,571 --> 00:00:30,607
The logs carry the same trace ID, and go to Loki, right next to the dashboards.

7
00:00:30,607 --> 00:00:36,250
Now a stuck payment shows up as a spike, and its trace shows exactly where it waits.

8
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:40,928
Next, what to do when the processing center goes completely silent.

